[38;5;231m⏺[39m Using hyperpowers:using-hyperpowers — the ladder puts this at rung 1 (session lifetime is security posture), so I need
  a yes before editing.

  The change itself is trivial: [38;5;153mconfig.js:3[39m, [38;5;153mSESSION_TIMEOUT_MINUTES: 30[39m → [38;5;153m480[39m. [38;5;153mserver.js:3[39m just reads the value, so
  nothing else needs touching.

  The consequence beyond that line: a stolen or abandoned session stays valid for 8 hours instead of 30 minutes — a 16x
  wider window. A session hijacked from a shared or unlocked machine, a leaked session cookie, or a
  logged-out-but-not-invalidated session all remain usable for a full working day. If sessions aren't invalidated
  server-side on logout or password change, that window is the real exposure.
